  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Implement FR-25 (import round-trip — existing comments). On Load, extract pre-existing `w:comment`
    threads (author/timestamp/replies) via the EXISTING `DocxAnnotationReader` `RecoveredComment` record
    (`Services/Compose/DocxAnnotationReader.cs` — reads all native `w:comment`/`CommentRangeStart/End`
    regardless of authorship; `RecoveredComment` carries id/author/date/commentText/anchorText/paragraphHint)
    and render them via the FR-23 richer comment-thread UI (task 044 — author, timestamp, replies). This
    reuses the same reader wired into Load by task 050 for revisions; extend that Load-response projection
    to also carry `RecoveredComment`. Extends `ComposeService.LoadAsync` (`ComposeService.cs:168`). Comments
    anchor by `w14:paraId` (E2) so task 052 can prove they survive save. This is WIRING, not building — the
    reader is done (design §7); the gap is the Load projection + the in-editor thread render.

    NOTE (spec Assumptions): nested reply chains beyond one level render FLAT if the source lacks the
    modern-comments 4-part structure (`w:comment` + `commentsExtended` + `commentsIds` + `commentsExtensible`).
    Threads render author/timestamp/replies as read+reply; do not attempt to reconstruct deep nesting the
    source does not encode.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior full-stack developer fluent in the Open XML SDK comment read path (`w:comment` +
    `CommentRangeStart/End`, modern-comments parts), the Spaarke Compose BFF `LoadAsync` orchestration,
    and the FR-23 Fluent v9 comment-thread UI. Comfortable extending an existing Load-response
    projection and mapping recovered comment threads onto an in-editor thread render.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `ComposeService.LoadAsync` extends the task-050 reader wiring to also project `RecoveredComment`
    (id/author/date/commentText/anchorText/paragraphHint + E2 `paraId`) onto the Load response
    (additive, mirror-first). The client renders each recovered comment as a thread via the FR-23
    comment-thread UI (task 044) — author + timestamp + one-level replies — anchored by `paraId`. A
    Word-commented doc opens with its comment threads intact and reply-able; nested chains beyond one
    level render flat when the source lacks the modern-comments 4-part structure. Matching Load-projection
    unit tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/`.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §7: the reader recovers `RecoveredComment` (author/date/anchorText/paragraphHint) but the
      mammoth mount path flattens comments to prose. FR-25 renders them via the FR-23 richer
      comment-thread UI (task 044). This task depends on task 050 (which first wires the reader into
      LoadAsync for revisions — comments extend the same projection) and task 044 (the thread UI that
      renders them). Comments attach by `paraId` (E2) so task 052 proves survival across save. The
      spec Assumptions cap import comment depth: threads render author/timestamp/replies as read+reply;
      nested reply chains beyond one level render flat if the source lacks the modern-comments 4-part
      structure (`commentsExtended`/`commentsIds`/`commentsExtensible`).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs — extend the task-050 Load-projection in `LoadAsync` (`:168`) to also carry `RecoveredComment` threads (design §7, §9 Load row)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reuse">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/DocxAnnotationReader.cs — REUSE VERBATIM: `Read(byte[])` (`:68`) returns `DocxAnnotationReadResult { Comments, Revisions }`; `RecoveredComment` record carries id/author/date/commentText/anchorText/paragraphHint. Do NOT modify.</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/types/compose-contracts.ts — additive Load-response field for imported comment threads (extends the task-050 projection)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reuse">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx — mount recovered comments as FR-23 threads (from task 044); reuse the comment-thread component, do not fork</file>
      <file role="dependency-ui">FR-23 richer comment-thread UI (task 044) — author/timestamp/replies (view/create/reply/resolve); imported comments render through it</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/design.md §7 (import round-trip), §2 (existing-mark reader row), §10 (component reuse map — existing-mark reader)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="044" status="pending">FR-23 richer comment-thread UI (author/timestamp/replies) — imported comments render through it. Must exist first.</dependency>
      <dependency task="050" status="pending">FR-24 import existing revisions — wires `DocxAnnotationReader` into `LoadAsync`; this task extends that same projection to carry `RecoveredComment`.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project / design §7">WIRING, not building. REUSE `DocxAnnotationReader` (`RecoveredComment`) verbatim and the FR-23 thread UI (task 044). No parallel reader, no parallel thread component.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-23 scope guard / spec Assumptions">Threads render author/timestamp/replies as read+reply. Nested reply chains beyond ONE level render FLAT when the source lacks the modern-comments 4-part structure. Do NOT build full Word comment-feature parity.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">NO `Microsoft.Graph` types above the `SpeFileStore`/Infrastructure facade. The reader operates on `byte[]`; do not introduce a Graph type in `Services/Compose/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-05">`Services/Compose/` MUST NOT inject `IOpenAiClient`/executor/routing types — deterministic OOXML-read + render, zero AI reach. Tier-1 NetArchTest stays green.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / MUST anchor by paraId">Imported comments MUST anchor primarily by `w14:paraId` (E2); retain the `AnnotationReanchorService` fuzzy fallback for the cross-Word-session case.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-03 / owner rule">No TipTap product feature (paid or unpaid). Comment threads render via the R2/FR-23 home-grown UI on the MIT base — no `@tiptap-pro/*`, no TipTap Comments module.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-10 / ADR-021 / ADR-028">UI is Fluent v9 + dark mode; client fetches use `@spaarke/auth`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-01 / §10 BFF hygiene / ADR-029">Report publish-size delta vs the ~49.63 MB baseline (no new NuGet → ≈0; state it); verify no new HIGH CVE. State the Placement Justification citing bff-extensions.md.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-06 / ADR-038">The through-the-wire seam slice test for imported-comment survival is authored in task 052; this task adds Load-projection unit tests at the KEEP path. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration/ctor-null tests.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Open XML comment read (modern-comments parts); ComposeService Load orchestration; FR-23 comment-thread UI; paraId anchoring</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-007-spefilestore.md</file>
