      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Comment reader (reuse verbatim)" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/DocxAnnotationReader.cs">
        `Read(byte[])` (`:68`) returns `DocxAnnotationReadResult.Comments` — `RecoveredComment { Id, Author, Date, CommentText, AnchorText, ParagraphHint }`. Extend the task-050 Load-projection to carry these; do not touch the reader.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Comment-thread UI reuse" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx">
        Render imported comments through the FR-23 thread component (task 044) — author/timestamp/one-level replies. Reuse, do not fork.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + dependency check">Declare rigor (FULL). Confirm deps 044 (thread UI) + 050 (reader wired into Load) are ✅. Load bff-extensions.md + ADRs. Read design §7 + the reader `RecoveredComment` shape; do NOT plan any reader change.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Extend the Load-response projection for comments">Add an additive `importedComments` (or equivalent) field to the Load-response contract (mirror-first) carrying `RecoveredComment` fields + the E2 `paraId`. Reuse the `RecoveredComment` shape; empty list (not null) when no comments.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Project comments in LoadAsync">Extend the task-050 reader call in `LoadAsync` to also map `DocxAnnotationReadResult.Comments` onto the response, attaching the paraId from the E2 pre-parse map (task 010).</step>
    <step order="3" name="Render threads via FR-23 UI">In `ComposeEditor.tsx`, mount recovered comments as FR-23 threads (task 044) — author, timestamp, one-level replies — anchored by paraId. Do NOT add a TipTap Comments module.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Depth cap">Render author/timestamp/replies as read+reply. If the source lacks the modern-comments 4-part structure, render nested chains beyond one level FLAT (spec Assumptions) — document the behavior, do not reconstruct deep nesting.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Anchor + fuzzy fallback">Anchor by paraId first; retain the `AnnotationReanchorService` fuzzy fallback for the cross-Word-session case.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Unit tests + verify">Add Load-projection unit tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/` (Word-commented fixture → threads with author/timestamp + paraId; flat-render for a source without modern-comments parts; empty list for no comments). Build BFF + shared lib; run NetArchTest facade check; report publish-size delta (~0) + CVE + Placement Justification; update TASK-INDEX.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs (LoadAsync projects RecoveredComment threads)</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/types/compose-contracts.ts (additive imported-comments field)</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx (imported comments rendered as FR-23 threads)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/ (comment Load-projection tests)</output>
    <output type="report">Publish-size delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline; CVE scan; NetArchTest facade result; Placement Justification</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">A Word-commented `.docx` opens in Compose with its comment threads intact — author + timestamp visible, reply-able — rendered via the FR-23 thread UI (FR-25 acceptance).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`LoadAsync` reuses the EXISTING `DocxAnnotationReader` `RecoveredComment` (reader unmodified) and projects id/author/date/commentText/anchorText + paraId onto the Load response; a no-comment doc yields an empty list, not null.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Nested reply chains beyond one level render FLAT when the source lacks the modern-comments 4-part structure (spec Assumptions); the behavior is documented, not silently dropped.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Imported comments anchor primarily by `w14:paraId` (E2) with the fuzzy fallback retained; threads render through the FR-23 UI on the MIT base — no `@tiptap-pro/*`, no TipTap Comments module (NFR-03).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`Services/Compose/` injects no AI-internal type (NetArchTest green); no `Microsoft.Graph` type in `Services/Compose/` (ADR-007).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size reported absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB (≈0; no new NuGet); no new HIGH CVE; Placement Justification stated citing bff-extensions.md.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Load-projection unit tests exist at the KEEP path and pass; BFF + shared-lib builds green (no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI/ctor-null tests — ADR-038).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

